    "updated_at": "2026-09-06T19:03:38Z",
    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #306\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed branch `bb/relay-276-review-debt-11-12-serialize-view-reord-thr_eu3vn8cbxt` to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nAddressed the three lower-severity findings from issue #276:\n\n1. **`viewItemsStore.ts`** — `reorderViewItem` now takes the same view-level `SELECT id FROM views WHERE id = $1 FOR UPDATE` lock that `addViewItem` takes, as its first statement, before the row-level lock on the moved item. Carried over the explanatory comment style.\n2. **`viewQuery.ts`** — dropped the redundant `parseFilterNode(config.filter)` call. Hoisted `const filterNode = config.filter` and built both `filterProperties` and the `buildFilterSql` hook off that one narrowed binding, so `compileFilterNode` receives the already-validated `FilterNode` directly.\n3. **`driftCheck.ts`** — `generatePermissionManifest` now runs inside the same `withTransaction` that performs the orphan check and writes the notification, using that transaction's client; the separate pool checkout/release is gone, so both reads see one schema snapshot.\n\nAdded a concurrency test in `views.test.ts` that drives 20 trials of two parallel `chokePoint.reorderViewItem` calls against the real pool and asserts no two view items ever end up sharing a position.\n\nVerification this turn: `pnpm -r run build` (TypeScript build across all 7 backend workspace packages) succeeded with no errors, and the full backend test suite (`npx vitest run`) passed — 24 test files, 314 tests, all green.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
